1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja,
 
Yes, dear viewers,

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Vê carê jî em li gundekî navçeya Mabeta.
 
This time we are in a village in the Mabeta district.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Vê carê jî em ê derbasî du gunda bibin.
 
This time too, we will visit two villages.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Du gund bûnî yek.
 
Two villages that became one.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Gundê Elî Caro û gundê Raco.
 
The village of Eli Caro and the village of Raco.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Di vê heftiyê jî em bi hevrê derbas bibin.
 
Let's visit them together this week too.

7
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, îro jî em derbasî gundê Raco û Elî
Caro bûn.
 
Yes, dear viewers, today we went to the village of Raco and
Ali Caro.

8
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Îro jî em derbasî du gunda bûn.
 
Today we entered two villages.

9
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Milêtê her gunda jî li hev kom bûn.
 
The people of both villages gathered together.

10
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Naha jî em li gundê Racone.
 
Right now we are in the village of Raco.

11
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Naha em ê dîroka her gunda nas bikin.
 
Now we will learn about the history of both villages.

12
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Merheba ji we re.
 
Hello to you.

13
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Ehlen wa sehlen, bi hatina we.
 
Welcome, it's good to have you here.

14
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Hûn bi xêr hatin roniya çava.
 
You are welcome, light of our eyes.

15
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Spas, em te destpêkê te nas bikin.
 
Thank you, let's get to know you first.

16
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Navê min Mistefa ye, lawê Ezdîn, ez ji Elî Caro me.
 
My name is Mustafa, son of Ezdin, I'm from Ali Caro.

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Ser çavê min. Tu ji Elî Caro ye.
 
Upon my eyes. You are from Ali Caro.

18
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Elî Caro nav ji kû hatiye?
 
Where did the name Ali Caro come from?

19
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Bi xwedê jarek.
 
By God, a poor man.

20
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Navê wî bû Elî.
 
His name was Ali.

21
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Wî kirikirin Eliyê Jare.
 
They made it Ali the Poor.

22
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Elî Carû, bi Erebî dibêjin Elî Carû, bi Kurmancî jî dibêjin
Eliyê Jare.
 
Ali Caru, in Arabic they say Ali Caru, in Kurmanji they say
Ali the Poor.

23
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Naha em li vê derê ku em li gundê we û Raco jî, gihîştinê
hev du gund bûne yek.
 
Now here where we are in your village and Raco, you've
reached each other, two villages have become one.

24
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Dema ez derbasî gund bûm, min nizane kijan gund a ye.
 
When I entered the village, I didn't know which village it
is.

25
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Kîjan Elî Caro ye kîjan Raco ye. Bi rastî we ye yan na?
 
Which one is Ali Caro and which one is Raco. Is that true or
not?

26
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Mabîna me Elî Caro û Raco bes camî ye.
 
Between us, Ali Caro and Raco, there is only a mosque.

27
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Hali camiyê, xerbî Elî Caro ye, hali girda şerqî Raco ye.
 
The western side of the mosque is Ali Caro, and the eastern
side is Raco.

28
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Yanî bes camî di ortê me de ye. Wekî din gundê me ye.
 
So there is only a mosque in the middle. Otherwise, it is
our village.

29
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Naha Elî Caro, malbat yek e. Yan gellek malbat jî hene.
 
Now Ali Caro, is it one family? Or are there many families?

30
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Bi xwedê mala Hesûn e. Mala Hecbirîm, mala Eme.
 
By God, it's the family of Hasun. The family of Hecbirim,
the family of Eme.

31
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Mala Ehmed, mala Şêx e.
 
The family of Ahmed, the family of Sheikh.

32
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Ev ne esasî wanan yek in? An belavbûyî ne.
 
Aren't these originally one? Or are they spread out.

33
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Evna gî yek in.
 
They are all one.

34
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Evna gi kurê Eliyê Jare ne.
 
They are all the sons of Ali the Poor.

35
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Yanî gi yek in, aîle yek e.
 
So they are all one, the family is one.

36
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Wekî din gî pismam û dotmam e. Tev bi hevtinê re pir in.
 
Besides that, they are all cousins. They are all close to
each other.

37
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Dibistan jî yek e.
 
The school is also one.

38
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Dibistan, sala hezar û nehsad û pêncî û heşta de hatiye
girtin.
 
The school was opened in 1958.

39
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Kalê min mixtar bû. Wî girtin da.
 
My grandfather was the mukhtar. He got it opened.

40
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Sala hezar û nehsed û pêncî û heşta.
 
The year 1958.

41
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Ku qeçkê me deran ko xwendin, dera xwendin.
 
When our children went to study, they went there.

42
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Wê çaxê mekteba me xwendin pênc gund de.
 
Back then, five villages studied at our school.

43
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Li wê derê dixwînin, heya şefî çara.
 
They study there up to fourth grade.

44
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Yanî dibistan yek e, mizgeft yek e.
 
So the school is one, the mosque is one.

45
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Civak yek e, yanî hemî tişt bi hevre ne.
 
The society is one, so everything is together.

46
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Mabîna me û Raco gî yek e.
 
Between us and Raco everything is one.

47
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Heta naha ku komîna me yek e.
 
Even now, our commune is one.

48
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Komîn jî yek e?
 
Is the commune one too?

49
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Komîna me jî yek e.
 
Our commune is also one.

50
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Navê komîna we jî kîjan şehîd e?
 
Which martyr is your commune named after?

51
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Bi xwedê şehîde Xoşnav.
 
By God, Martyr Xoshnav.

52
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Navê komîna me ye.
 
It's the name of our commune.

53
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Spas ji te re apê mi.
 
Thank you my uncle.

54
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Spas ji te re jî spas.
 
Thank you to you too.

55
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Spas.
 
Thank you.

56
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Merheba apê min.
 
Hello my uncle.

57
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Merheba, ehlen we sehlen.
 
Hello, welcome.

58
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Em te jî nas bikin destpêkê.
 
Let's get to know you first too.

59
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Elî Hamiye.
 
Ali Hami.

60
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Ser çava min, tu ji Raco yî?
 
Upon my eyes, are you from Raco?

61
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Erê bi xwedê, Raco me.
 
Yes, by God, I am from Raco.

62
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
E ka hinekî ji mere ser gundê Raco biaxife.
 
Well, tell us a bit about the village of Raco.

63
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Raco çêkiriye da çêbûye, nav ji ku hatiye?
 
How did Raco get established, where did the name come from?

64
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Ya sîdî, Raco bi xwedê ... lêwê çûme zinê...
 
Sir, Raco by God... when I went there...

65
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Yanî ew ê ku hatîye vêrnê, navê wî Rac bû?
 
So the one who came here, his name was Rac?

66
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Rac bû. Rac bi xwedê lêwê çûme zinê.
 
It was Rac. Rac, by God, went to those hills.

67
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Û qeçkê Raco çar in.
 
And Rac has four children.

68
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Yek jê re dibêjin Hem, yek jî Nas.
 
One is called Hem, and one Nas.

69
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Yek jî Henan, yek jî His.
 
And one Henan, and one His.

70
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Evna qeçkê Raco ne.
 
These are Raco's children.

71
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Û Rac… Raco bi xwe, lawê Çomezîne.
 
And Rac... Raco himself, is the son of Chomezin.

72
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Û hat çi... li heya rûta ser kaniya rûta rûnişt.
 
And he came and settled on the bare hills above the bare
spring.

73
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Ji wir jî hat, wekî mezinê me dibêjin
 
From there he came, as our elders say,

74
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Çû li gundê Raco rûnişt, haviya Raco û ser Raco.
 
He went and settled in the village of Raco, around Raco and
on top of Raco.

75
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Çar lawê Raco hene, wekî min gotî.
 
Raco has four sons, as I said.

76
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Ev çar lavane, His û Henan û Hem û û yekî din Nas.
 
These four sons, His, Henan, Hem, and another one, Nas.

77
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Ev li kîderê rûniştine?
 
Where did they settle?

78
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Evna di gund dane.
 
They are in the village.

79
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Hemî di gundane?
 
All of them in the village?

80
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Hemî di gundane, bes qeçkê xwa hene.
 
All of them in the village, but they have their own
children.

81
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Qeçkê qeçka hene li wêderê.
 
There are grandchildren there.

82
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Em bi xwa ji Hamê ne.
 
We ourselves are from Hame.

83
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Malbata keja, Henên e.
 
The Keja family is from Hanen.

84
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Yanî dîsa ew yek in.
 
So they are one again.

85
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Giştik yek in, em malbat gi yek in bes.
 
They are all one, we families are all one.

86
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Çaxê Elî Caro ku navê yekî din hatîya, nav kî jan malbat e?
 
As for Ali Caro, since another name has come up, which
family is it?

87
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Belê, bes du mal di nav me de li vir ...
 
Yes, but there are two houses among us here...

88
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Ji derveyî gund hatine, henê dibêjin Şera û mala Bekirê
Reşo, ji Gurda hatine wêderê.
 
They came from outside the village, some call them Shera and
the house of Bekirê Resho, they came from Gurda over there.

89
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Evna ne ji Raco ne. Bes em mezin da ne, hevdû da em bi hevre
ne ye
 
These are not from Raco. But we grew up together, we are
with each other.

90
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
E naha hejmara gund, çiqas mal e?
 
And now the number in the village, how many houses are
there?

91
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Gund teqrîben şêst mal e, pêncî şêst mal e.
 
The village is approximately sixty houses, fifty-sixty
houses.

92
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Û Elî Caro?
 
And Ali Caro?

93
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Elî Caro, ew ji sê çel mal heye.
 
Ali Caro, it also has around thirty-forty houses.

94
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Çel mal in?
 
Forty houses?

95
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Ew ji şêst mal e...
 
That is also sixty houses...

96
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Yanî ev gund sed û bîst an
 
So these villages are one hundred and twenty or

97
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Haaa wasan, sed û deh e, sed û bîst yan nagihê sed û sî
malî.
 
Yea exactly, one hundred and ten, one hundred and twenty, or
doesn't reach one hundred and thirty houses.

98
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Em dibînin ku şadîyek a mirova di keve?
 
Does that mean when someone is happy?

99
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Hemî bi hevre jiyan dikin, şahîya ve li miriya ve,
 
Everyone lives together, at weddings and funerals,

100
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Em gi da bi hevre ne.
 
We are all together in this.

101
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Komîn, wekî hûn di zanin, Mistefa gotîye. Komîna me gi yek
e, vira me gi yek e, em giştik bi hevre ne.
 
Commune, as you know, Mustafa said it. Our commune is all
one, everything here is one, we are all together.

102
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Mala ve ava be.
 
Bless your house.

103
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Mala we jî ava be.
 
Bless your house too.

104
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Emê naha derbasî gundê we hemûyan jî bibin.
 
We will now pass through all of your village.

105
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Spas ji we re jî.
 
With pleasure.

106
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Spas ji we re jî.
 
Thank you to you too.

107
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Spas, ser çava.
 
Thank you, on my eyes.

108
00:05:52,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Ser seran.
 
Welcome.

109
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Gundê Elî Caro û Raco girêdayî navçeya Mabetayê ne.
 
The villages of Ali Caro and Raco are connected to the
district of Mabeta.

110
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Nêzî panzdeh kîlometreyan li rojavayê Mabetayê dikevin.
 
They are located about fifteen kilometers west of Mabeta.

111
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Gundê Elî Caro û gundê Raco bûne yek gund.
 
The village of Ali Caro and the village of Raco have become
one village.

112
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Û malên wan gihîştin e hev du.
 
And their houses have joined together.

113
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Goristan, dibistan û komîna wan yek e.
 
Their cemetery, school, and commune are one.

114
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
Gundê Elî Caro û Raco, li ser çiyayekî bi navê
 
The villages of Ali Caro and Raco are on a mountain named

115
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Gêyaza zêra hatine ava kirin.
 
Geyaza Zera.

116
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Di nav Herêmeke çiyayî de ne.
 
They are in a mountainous region.

117
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Ev çiya bi darên zeytûnan xemilandî ne.
 
These mountains are adorned with olive trees.

118
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Her wekî tê gotin,
 
As it is said,

119
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Ku di demên berê de, hemû daristanên mêrxî bûn.
 
In the past, they were all pine forests.

120
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Û ta niha jî hinek daristan, li derdora gund hene û hawirekî
bedew pêk tînin.
 
And even now, there are some forests around the village,
creating a beautiful environment.

121
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Navê gundê Elî Caro ji navê kesekî bi navê Eliyê Jarî
hatiye.
 
The name of the village Ali Caro comes from the name of a
person called Aliye Jari.

122
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Ji Eliyê Jarî, te te ro ji wî çar kur çêdibin.
 
From Aliye Jari, four sons were born.

123
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Hacbirîm, Os, Ehmed û Şêxê.
 
Hacbirim, Os, Ahmed, and Shexe.

124
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Û bi vî awayî gund mezin dibe.
 
And in this way, the village grows.

125
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Û koka wan jî ji êla biyan e.
 
And their roots are from the Biyan tribe.

126
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Gundê Elî Caro, ji şêst xanî pêk tê, û nêzî pênsed kes lê
dijîn.
 
The village of Ali Caro consists of sixty houses, and about
five hundred people live there.

127
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:19,000
Navê gundê Raco, ji kesekî bi navê Raco Mezin hatiye.
 
The name of the village Raco comes from a person named Raco
Mezin.

128
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,000
Ku ew weke damezrînerê gund tê naskirin,
 
Who is known as the founder of the village,

129
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Ango kesê yekemîn li gund niştecîh bûye.
 
Meaning he was the first person to settle in the village.

130
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Tê gotin ku sê kurên Raco Mezin hebûn.
 
It is said that Raco Mezin had three sons.

131
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Yek ji wan bi navê Nas Raco, li vir ma.
 
One of them, named Nas Raco, stayed here.

132
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Yê din jî çû li gundê Sewliyê li Navçeya Etmê niştecî bû.
 
Another went to settle in the village of Sewliye in the Atma
district.

133
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Û naha ew bi malbata kurdî têne nas kirin.
 
And now they are known as the Kurdish family.

134
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Û yê sêyemîn bi navê Heme Raco
 
And the third one, named Hame Raco

135
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Li devereke nêzî Raco niştecî bû ye,
 
Settled in an area near Raco,

136
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Û nav lê bûye gundê Raco.
 
And it was named the village of Raco.

137
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Sê malbatên bingehiyen ku dera cada heye
 
There are three main families where the road is

138
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Osî, Hemeraco û Malbata Wahîd.
 
Osi, Hameraco, and the Wahid family.

139
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Ango bi gîştî, derdora nod xanî,
 
Meaning in total, around ninety houses,

140
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Û nêzî hezar û sed kes
 
And nearly one thousand one hundred people

141
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Li herdû gundan dijîn.
 
Live in both villages.

142
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Û her du gund, weke gundekî ne.
 
And both villages are like one village.

143
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja di gundê Elî Caro de jî em derbasî cem
mixtar bûn.
 
Yes dear viewers, in the village of Ali Caro we went to the
mukhtar.

144
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Cem Apê Remzî. Naha em bi hev re Apê Remzî jî nas bikin.
 
To Uncle Remzi. Now let's get to know Uncle Remzi together.

145
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Apê Remzî, jî leşkeriya Fransayê kiriye.
 
Uncle Remzi has also served in the French military.

146
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Merheba ji we re.
 
Hello to you.

147
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Ehlen û sehlen.
 
Welcome.

148
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Apê Remzî?
 
Uncle Remzi?

149
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Emrî te çiqas sal e?
 
Go ahead.

150
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Emrî te çiqas sal e?
 
How old are you?

151
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Wallah nizanim.
 
By God, I don't know.

152
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Ez difikirim ku ez ketim salên heştêyan.
 
I think I am in my eighties.

153
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:40,000
Dema tu bûyî leşker, tu eskeriya Fransa kirî, tê bîra te?
 
When you were a soldier, you served in the French military,
do you remember?

154
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

155
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Dêmek
 
That means

156
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Emrê min daxwaz bû
 
My age was requested

157
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Ez ji Tirkiyê revîm û hatim
 
I fled from Turkey and came

158
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Ez bûm eskerê Fransayê. Û min çar sala eskeriya Fransa kir.
 
I became a soldier for France. And I served as a French
soldier for four years.

159
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Tu li kû derê bû, li bakur, tu li nêzîk bûyî?
 
Where were you, in the north, were you near?

160
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Li baderê
 
Out there

161
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Li Efrîn, li Ezazê.
 
In Afrin, in Azaz.

162
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Mantiqeya Ezazê
 
The Azaz region

163
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Heta li Çobanbegê
 
Up to Çobanbey

164
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Heta Cerablusê
 
Up to Jarablus

165
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:09,000
Min li balê mantiqa eskerî dikir.
 
I served in the military region there.

166
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Yanî tê bîra te tu kîjan wextî da bû, tu kîjan salê de bûyî?
 
Do you remember what time it was, what year you served?

167
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Wallah ya îlahî
 
By God, oh my Lord

168
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Kî li bê çaxê
 
Who remembers

169
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Sala dipirsî û li esasa dipirsî,
 
If you asked the year and asked for the basis,

170
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Her kes kîfa xwe dikir
 
Everyone was enjoying themselves

171
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Te çar sala eskerî dikir?
 
You served in the military for four years?

172
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Çar salan min cem Fransayê eskerî kir.
 
I served with the French military for four years.

173
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:34,000
E havêlê te wextî kî bû? Kes ji gundê te, ji mantiqê te kes
hebû?
 
Who was your friend at that time? Was there anyone from your
village, from your region?

174
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Hevalên min, ji gundê me, tune ne.
 
My friends, from our village, there are none.

175
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Ji kû derê hebûn?
 
Where were they from?

176
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Ji mantiqa em hebûn, mantiqa Bilbilê hebûn.
 
There were people from our region, there were people from
the Bilbil region.

177
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Ji mantiqa Bilbilê hebûn,
 
There were people from the Bilbil region,

178
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Wekî din tu piraqê me xilî, min û kesî Fransayê re nekir.
 
Otherwise, you cross our bridge, me and anyone else didn't
do it with France.

179
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Dibêjin wextê te da leşkerê Fransa...
 
They say during your time the French military...

180
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Dema ku kurmanc pir bûn da jê ra ew kirin, Fransa kirin?
 
When there were many Kurmanjis, did the French make them do
that?

181
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Ê kurmanc.
 
Yes, Kurmanjis.

182
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Yanî kurmanc di nav da hebûn, pir bûn?
 
So there were Kurmanjis among them, were there many?

183
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Ê kurmanc. Demek eskadronek vê ra digotin eskadron kurd,
lejê, nav lê nan.
 
Yes, Kurmanjis. They formed a squadron and named it the
Kurdish Squadron, the Legion.

184
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Wextê bi herbê Çolê ra kirin, Fransa herb bi Çolê ra kirin.
 
When they fought the war with Çolo, the French fought the
war with Çolo.

185
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Çolox neşikandin, nekuştin.
 
They did not defeat or kill Çolo.

186
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Çolox kuştin, rabûn kirin eskadron lejê kurd lêxe. Seke.
 
To kill Çolo, they got the Kurdish Legion Squadron to attack
him.

187
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Yanî kurmancan mêrxasî xistin. Heta bi Fransa bi ewa kir.
 
I mean, the Kurmanjis fought bravely. Even with the French.

188
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Yanî negotin Çolox kurmancan kuştin, gotin eskadron kurd
lejê lêxe.
 
They didn't say Kurmanjis killed Çolo, they said the Kurdish
Legion Squadron attacked him.

189
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Yanî çi maneyê dide?
 
I mean, what does that mean?

190
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Yanî manesiya xwe kurmancan mêrxasî kirin.
 
It means the Kurmanjis showed bravery.

191
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Kurmancan mêrxasiya xwe kuştin Çoloq anîn.
 
The Kurmanjis fought bravely, they killed Çolo and brought
him down.

192
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Ewa misteşariya Fransa ew awa da laqaba wan.
 
The French advisors gave them that nickname.

193
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Kurmanca?
 
The Kurmanjis?

194
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Kurmanca.
 
The Kurmanjis.

195
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Ê dema ku ew şer çêbûye bi Çolê te bîra te?
 
Do you remember when that war with Çolo happened?

196
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Ne tê bîra min, bes wê çaxê gotin mezinên me o.
 
I don't remember, but our elders talked about it.

197
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Û wextê ku Çoloq ku herbê bike, hat di cem bavikê min ra
derbas bû.
 
And when Çolo was going to fight the war, he came and passed
by my father.

198
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Demek bavikê min li vir bû, Çolox di bera ra derbas bû.
 
My father was here, and Çolo passed right by him.

199
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Ê Çolox çû li wê mir, li topraxê Çeqelê mir.
 
Çolo went and died there, he died on the lands of Çeqel.

200
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Li wê derê kuştin.
 
They killed him right there.

201
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Ê di wê demê da Çoloq bi Mihedînê Îbşaşî bû, di wê demê da
evna li hember Fransa şer dikirin?
 
Was Çolo with Mihedînê Îbşaşî at that time? Were they
fighting against the French?

202
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Na, na, na, ê Mihedînê Îbşaşî bariya wî ye, bariya wî ye.
 
No, no, no, Mihedînê Îbşaşî was before him, he was before
him.

203
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Bariya Çolê ye, Mihedînê Îbşaşî.
 
Mihedînê Îbşaşî was before Çolo.

204
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Yanî wî jî li hember Fransa şer kir?
 
So he fought against the French too?

205
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Wî jî kir.
 
He did too.

206
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Yanî ê destpêkê şer li hember Fransa kirî, Mihiyê Îbşaşî bû?
 
So the first one to fight against the French was Mihiyê
Îbşaşî?

207
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Ê, paşê Fransa Çolêx kir...
 
Yes, then the French... then Çolo fought.

208
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Çolox demek di wê de, di geryayî komreşê de, digerya ewê de
mir.
 
Çolo was around there, wandering in Komreş, he was wandering
and died there.

209
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Ê piştî wî, te bûyî eskerê Fransa?
 
And after him, were you a French soldier?

210
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Piştî wî em bûn eskeriya Fransa.
 
After him, we served in the French army.

211
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Demek Evdo birakê xwe bû, birakê Çolêx bû. Evdo kuştin, paşê
ew kuştin. Paşê Çoloq kuştin.
 
Evdo was his brother, he was Çolo's brother. They killed
Evdo, then they killed him. Then they killed Çolo.

212
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Wê demê eskerê xwe pir bûn?
 
Were there many soldiers back then?

213
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Demek wê çaxê eskerê kurmanc taîn kiribûn, ji Qiriqxaneyê
hatin lê Çolê xistin.
 
At that time, they had assigned Kurmanji soldiers, they came
from Kırıkhan and attacked Çolo.

214
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Ji paş ra hatin.
 
They came from behind.

215
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Yanî di wê demê da ji Qiriqxaneyê hatin li Çolê xistin?
 
I mean, did they come from Kırıkhan and attack Çolo at that
time?

216
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Ji Qiriqxaneyê hatin.
 
They came from Kırıkhan.

217
00:12:52,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Demek wê çaxê Fransa eskerê xwe eskadronek... eskadronek vê
ra dibêjin, 100 esker e wê çaxê.
 
At that time, the French had a squadron of soldiers... a
squadron as they call it, it was 100 soldiers back then.

218
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Wê çaxê ji paş ra hatin, lê Çolê xistin.
 
At that time, they came from behind and attacked Çolo.

219
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Ji ewê da hatin, ji Încerliyê da hilkişîn hatin, Çoloq li wî
aliyê, dûziyê...
 
They came from there, they came up from İncirli and came to
Çolo on that side, in the plains...

220
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Ji paş ra hatin Çoloq xistin, Çoloq kuştin.
 
They came from behind and attacked Çolo, they killed Çolo.

221
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Ê çi tê bîra te, hîna di wê demê da çi çi bû?
 
What else do you remember? What else happened back then?

222
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Demek wê çaxê hîna em yanî, em digotin devê sê ye devê çar e
devê pênc e... anezam.
 
Back then, we were just kids, around thirteen, fourteen,
fifteen... I don't know.

223
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Yanî di 13 sal, heya 15 salî di wê demê da?
 
You mean you were 13 to 15 years old at that time?

224
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
Ê, wê çaxê tê bîra min.
 
Yes, I remember that time.

225
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Apê Remzî, di wê demê da te got ez di Efrînê da bûm û tu
çûyî Cerablisê jî di wê demê da.
 
Uncle Remzî, you said you were in Afrin and also went to
Cerablus at that time.

226
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Te şer li hember kesî kir?
 
Did you fight against anyone?

227
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Na me tu şer nekir. Gund demek maxfera da bû.
 
No, we didn't fight at all. The village was like a police
station back then.

228
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Maxfera, teyîn dikirin, mesele Çobambeg tike ra Cerabulusê
tike re...
 
The station would make assignments, for example, a part to
Çobanbey and a part to Cerablus.

229
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Fransa hebe we teyîn ji Fransa da çêdibû.
 
As long as the French were there, the assignments were made
by the French.

230
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Fransa demek dirêj li vir ma. Tê bîra te dema ji vir derket
û çûye?
 
The French stayed here for a long time. Do you remember when
they left from here?

231
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Wextê ji vir derketî, wextê derketî
 
When they left here, when they left...

232
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Ev tişta ra bibim, demek li Cerablusê bûm.
 
Let me clarify this, I was in Cerablus then.

233
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Dema Fransa ji vir çû, di 46'an da ji vir çû. Di wê demê da
kê li hember şer kir?
 
When the French left here, they left in '46. Who fought
against them at that time?

234
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Kurmancan me nekir, qenê Ereban kirin.
 
We Kurmanjis didn't, the Arabs basically did.

235
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Kurdan li hember Fransa nedikir?
 
The Kurds didn't fight the French?

236
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Na Kurdan nekir.
 
No, the Kurds didn't.

237
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Kî bûn wê demê da?
 
Who were there at that time?

238
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Demek wê çaxê îşte Reşîdê Îbo hebû, Mhihê Îbşaşê li wê da
bû.
 
At that time, there was Reşîdê Îbo, and Mhihê Îbşaşê was
there.

239
00:14:56,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Berî wa ... berî Çoloq bû.
 
It was before them... before Çolo.

240
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Paşê Çoloq hat, paşê îşte pê ra hatin kurmanc.
 
Then Çolo came, and then the Kurmanjis joined in.

241
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Demek Mhihê Îbşaşe, ji berî Çolêx ra ye, nexwe berî ye,
belye.
 
So Mhihê Îbşaşê was before Çolo, of course he was before
him, yes.

242
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Na, ê eskeriya li Fransa kirina, di çiyayê kurmênc da, tu
nizanî kî kî ne? Te nav nas nakî, kî bûn?
 
Now, the ones who did military service for the French in the
Kurd-Dagh (Kurdish Mountain), don't you know who they were?
Don't you recognize any names, who were they?

243
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Kî kî? Nizanm, nemane ne...
 
Who and who? I don't know, none of them are left...

244
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Ji navçeya Şiyê hebûn, ji Bilbilê hebûn.
 
There were people from Shiye district, from Bilbil.

245
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Ji Bilbilê hebûn, ji Şiyê hebûn, ji Qitmê hebûn.
 
There were people from Bilbil, from Shiye, from Qitme.

246
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Ekseriyat ji Qitmê, ji Qurtqilaqê mezin û ji Qitmê hebûn.
 
The majority were from Qitme, from big Qurtqilaq, and from
Qitme.

247
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Ehmed Şêxo bû ji Qitmê?
 
Was Ehmed Şêxo from Qitme?

248
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:46,000
Ehmed Şêxo bû, erê. Ji Qurtqilaqê mezin ew bû, Ehmed Şêxo
bû.
 
Yes, it was Ehmed Şêxo. He was from big Qurtqilaq, it was
Ehmed Şêxo.

249
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Birak hebû Bedrî, birak jî hebû.
 
He had a brother named Bedri, he had a brother too.

250
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
Apê Remzî tu kîjan çax bûyî muxtar?
 
Uncle Remzi, when did you become a mukhtar?

251
00:15:53,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Li dora Hafiz Esed, ku înqilab kirin.
 
Around the time of Hafez al-Assad, when they made the coup.

252
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Yanî di 70'yî da.
 
I mean, in the 70s.

253
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
70'yî salan da.
 
In the 70s.

254
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Tu muxtarê 6 gundan bûyî?
 
Were you the mukhtar of 6 villages?

255
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Erê. Hezvera yek.
 
Yes. Hezvera is one.

256
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Mahsere dudu. Birka sisê.
 
Mahsere is two. Birka is three.

257
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Raca çar. Miste'şûra pênc.
 
Raca is four. Miste'şûra is five.

258
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:29,000
Em şeş gund in, Çomazna şeş. Em şeş gund in.
 
We are six villages, Çomazna is six. We are six villages.

259
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Tu muxtarê 6 gundan bûy? Û heya niha tu muxtarî?
 
You were the mukhtar of 6 villages? And you're still a
mukhtar?

260
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

261
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Serkeftin ji te ra.
 
I wish you success.

262
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Muxtar dema ku te bû muxtar heya niha, navên gundên we jî
hatin guherîn.
 
Mukhtar, from the time you became a mukhtar until now, the
names of your villages have also been changed.

263
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Yanî di wê demê da dewleta Sûriyê ji nav guhertin?
 
I mean, did the Syrian state change the names at that time?

264
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Ê sûriyê guhertin.
 
Yes, Syria changed them.

265
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Yanî guhartandina xwe, mesele Alîcaro, Alîcaro, esase. Esasa
gund e.
 
I mean, their changing... for example Alîcaro, Alîcaro is
the origin. It's the origin of the village.

266
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Şorê Tirkî jê derxistin. Ê Tirkî in... Mesele gundê me ha...
Mahsercix, Mahsere lêkirin. Cix rakirin.
 
They removed the Turkish words. The Turkish ones... For
example, our village... Mahsercix, they made it Mahsere.
They removed the "cix".

267
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Navê gundê we... hemû, çar caran bi nav bîn in.
 
The name of your village... they have been named four times.

268
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Destpêkê ku kurmancî bûn, piştî wê Roman hat, Aramiya da
dîsa nav guhertin,
 
At first they were Kurmanji, after that the Romans came,
they changed the names in Aramaic,

269
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Tirk hat dîsa guherî, Sûriyê hat dîsa guherî. Lê gund wekî
berê ma, nav wek berê ma...
 
The Turks came and changed them again, the Syrians came and
changed them again. But the village remained as before, the
names remained as before...

270
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Yanî her demî, hinek hatin navê gundên we guhertin?
 
So every time, someone came and changed the names of your
villages?

271
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

272
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Mala te ava be. Spas ji te ra.
 
Bless your house. Thank you.

273
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Ehlen û sehlen, bixêr silamet.
 
Welcome, have a safe and good time.

274
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Ser çavan.
 
You are most welcome.

275
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Herdu gund bi hev ra têkilî û peywendiyên baş danîne.
 
Both villages have established good relations and ties with
each other.

276
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:57,000
Di aheng şahî û xemgîniyan de bi hevdû ra alîkar in û
destekê didin hevdû.
 
In harmony, joy, and sorrow, they are helpful to each other
and support each other.

277
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Xelkên herdu gundan debara xwe bi çandiniyê dikin.
 
The people of both villages make their living through
farming.

278
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Mîna hemû gundên navçeyê, darên zeytûnê berhemên sereke ne.
 
Like all the villages in the district, olive trees are the
main crop.

279
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Li gel zeytûnan darên fêkî jî tên çandin.
 
Along with olives, fruit trees are also planted.

280
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Mamoste merheba êvara te baş.
 
Teacher hello, good evening.

281
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Merheba êvara we jî. Ehlen û sehlen. Ser serê min ser çavên
min.
 
Hello, good evening to you too. Welcome. You are most
welcome.

282
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Spasdar im. Em destpêkê te nas bikin?
 
Thank you. Can we get to know you first?

283
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Edhem, ji Alîcaro.
 
Edhem, from Alîcaro.

284
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Spasdar im ji te ra. Ser çavên min.
 
I am thankful to you. You are most welcome.

285
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Naha ev ciyê em lê, ev gelî bi vê bîrê tê naskirin? Wekî te
qise kir...
 
Now this place we are in, is this valley known by this well?
As you were talking about...

286
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Ev bîr, çend gundan li ser av dibirin? Çend gund av ji vê
bîrê dibirin yanî?
 
This well, how many villages took water from it? How many
villages took water from this well?

287
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Vê bîrê... bîra 7 gundan bû berê.
 
This well... was the well of 7 villages in the past.

288
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Heft gundan dihatin dibirin. Mahserkê, Birka, Çomazna, Raca,
 
Seven villages used to come and take it. Mahserkê, Birka,
Çomazna, Raca,

289
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Miste'şûra, haşxasê ku me gihayê, berê dihatin av ji vê bîrê
dibirin.
 
Miste'şûra, the people of our time, they used to come and
take water from this well.

290
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Av berê tune bû. Bes naha li gundan giyan bîr çêbûn, her kes
ava xwe dibe.
 
There was no water back then. But now all the villages have
wells, everyone takes their own water.

291
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:29,000
Vê bîrê jî xan û mahcûr ma naka wisa. Mehsalek we'deha tekra
me termîm kir.
 
And this well remained abandoned like this. A year ago we
restored it again.

292
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
Manî bîrek eserî ye, kevin e.
 
Meaning it's an ancient well, it's old.

293
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
Yanî wek ku komînê çêkir...
 
You mean like the commune built it...

294
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Em komînê me çêkir.
 
Our commune built it.

295
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Komîna gundê me ew kir, me çêkir me hazir kir.
 
Our village's commune did that, we built it, we prepared it.

296
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Naha ev gundê ku te behsa wî kirî, naha Miste'şûra li kû
derê dikeve?
 
Now, the village you mentioned, where is Miste'şûra located
now?

297
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Ev gundê ku te ji me ra got dema em derbasî gundê we bûn, ev
Miste'şûra li milê din da dikeve?
 
This village you told us about when we passed into your
village, does this Miste'şûra fall on the other side?

298
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Miste'şûra, ha wî devî ra nêzîk e.
 
Miste'şûra is close to that side.

299
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Devî ra dî, gelî ra nêzîk e. Dihatin vir, bi dewar dihatin
av dibirin.
 
It's close to the other side, near the valley. They used to
come here, they came with cattle and took water.

300
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Û ev gelî jî hemî bi vê bîrê tê naskirin?
 
And this entire valley is known by this well?

301
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Hemî bi vê bîrê tê naskirin. Geliyê bîrê.
 
It is all known by this well. The Valley of the Well.

302
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Ev bîra, kevine? Nû ye? Bîra çi ye?
 
So...

303
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Ev bîra, kevine? Nû ye? Bîra çi ye?
 
Is this well old? New? What is this well?

304
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Bîreka wisa, ne xirab e, yanî
 
A well like this, not bad, you know

305
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Emrê xwe pir dirêj e. Kes nizane ji çi wexta ye.
 
Its age is very long. No one knows from what time it is.

306
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Bes roman berî Selehedîn bûye, Selehedîn jî hezar û sêsed
sal e.
 
But the Romans were before Saladin, and Saladin is a
thousand and three hundred years ago.

307
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Vê bîrê û vê dara çinarê ha...
 
This well and this plane tree...

308
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:17,000
Hezar û sêsed sal teqrîben heye.
 
It has been roughly a thousand and three hundred years.

309
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Ê ji berê ev cihê Kurda ye? Piştî wî?
 
So from the beginning, this is a Kurdish place? After him?

310
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Ev cihê Kurda ye, tebîî...
 
This is a Kurdish place, of course...

311
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Her carê berê roman jî Kurd bûn, dû roman re jî Kurd e.
 
Always before the Romans they were Kurds, and after the
Romans they are Kurds.

312
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Belê. Niha te behsa darê kir. Ev dara, çinarê ye?
 
Yes. Now you mentioned the tree. This tree, is it a plane
tree?

313
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Çinar e, a.
 
It's a plane tree, yeah.

314
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Te got emrê wê çi qas e?
 
How old did you say it is?

315
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,000
Hezar û sêsed sal e.
 
It is one thousand three hundred years old.

316
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Dîrokek nivîsandine, kesî, yanî kesek lêkolîn kiriye?
 
Is there written history, by anyone, I mean has anyone
examined it?

317
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Na.
 
No.

318
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Bi devkî hatiye gotin?
 
It was said orally?

319
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Bi gotin a, tê gotin.
 
Orally, it is said.

320
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Tê gotin... Ev dara jî çiqas bilindbûna wê heye?
 
It is said... This tree, how tall is it?

321
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Bilindbûna wê teqrîben pencî metir bilindbûn zêde hebû.
 
It used to be roughly over fifty meters tall.

322
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:52,000
Bes millet hat qudkir, kirin êzing û giya,
 
But people came and cut it down, made it firewood and
branches,

323
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,000
an dar û gî-, qudkirin a...
 
or tree branches-, they cut it down...

324
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Bes dar pir mezin bû.
 
But the tree was very large.

325
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Na, ev kêlek...
 
Now, this side...

326
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Golik derbas dibû salekî, fînda dibû di koçka darê re.
 
A year-old calf would pass through the hollow of the tree.

327
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Naha hazir, l'tenişta me holî darê we da, belî, yanî halîk
hîn vekiriye.
 
Right now, next to us on that side of the tree, it is
visible, I mean there's still a hollow opening.

328
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Vekiriye.
 
It's open.

329
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
Niha ev kêlek dara çi ye? Ev mehsere ye?
 
Now, what is this beside the tree? Is this an olive press?

330
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:14,000
Hev a... meqbes e, zemçî çêker bû.
 
This is a... press, it used to make olive oil.

331
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Paşê jî girtin û naha wisa nîvî maye.
 
Later they closed it down and now it has remained halfway
done.

332
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Mehsere ye.
 
It's an olive press.

333
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Mamoste deha... te got başqe ji vê bîrê tune ne, ne?
 
Uncle, you said there are no others besides this well,
right?

334
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Tune ye, na.
 
There aren't, no.

335
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,000
Her vê tenê ye.
 
It's just this one.

336
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Û av jî tê da heye?
 
And there is water in it?

337
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Tê jî av.
 
There's water in it too.

338
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Ava wê qet huşk nabe.
 
Its water never dries up.

339
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Û biharê, ev di çêle da derdikeve,
 
And in the spring, the water comes out of the edge,

340
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Heta bihara meha şeşe, meha pênca, şeşe, dimîne hişk nabe.
 
It stays until spring, the sixth month, the fifth or sixth
month, it doesn't dry up.

341
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Av kaniya qut dibe.
 
The spring water stops.

342
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Ev ava baranê ye, yanî, dikeve vir a...
 
Is this rainwater, meaning, it falls in here...

343
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,000
Na, ava baranê nakeve.
 
No, rainwater doesn't fall into it.

344
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Ava wê jêr tê.
 
Its water comes from below.

345
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Çav e.
 
It's a spring.

346
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Ê ça ye.
 
Yeah, it's a spring.

347
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:50,000
Mal ava be, spasdar im.
 
Bless you, thank you.

348
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:53,000
Mal ava, ji ava, ser serê min, ser çavê min, hatine we pir
bi xêr hatin çavên min.
 
Bless you too, upon my head and eyes, you are very welcome.

349
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Spas, sax weş.
 
Thank you.

350
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
Saetê te jî xweş, ehlen wa sehlen.
 
Bless you too, welcome.

351
00:21:56,000 --> 00:22:05,000
Ser serê min.
 
Upon my head.

352
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:08,000
Li gundê Elî Rojawa bîreka avê heye,
 
In the village of Elî Rojawa, there is a water well,

353
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Bi navê Bîra Elî Carat tê naskirin.
 
It is known by the name of the Elî Carat Well.

354
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:15,000
Xelkê gund av jê dibirin û pez û xwar ji av didan.
 
The villagers used to take water from it and mostly watered
the livestock.

355
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:19,000
Û ta niha di hemû demsalan da av a wî dikişe,
 
And until now, water flows from it in all seasons,

356
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:37,000
Û di biharê da dibe cihê geşt û seyranê.
 
And in spring, it becomes a place for picnics and outings.

357
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:39,000
Apê Xelîl, merhaba stêra.
 
Uncle Xelîl, hello, stars.

358
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:43,000
Ehlan merhaba, tu bi xêr hatî, ronahîk da, ehlen û sehlen.
 
Hello. Welcome, bringing light... welcome...

359
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:46,000
Sax be, Apê Xelîl. Te dît her gundekî em digerin,
 
Bless you, Uncle Xelîl. You see, every village we visit,

360
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:52,000
Tiştekî wan yê balkêş, çi hebe, kesekî necar be, yanî çi kar
dike gundî da hebe em çêdikin.
 
Whatever interesting things they have, if there's a
carpenter, meaning whatever work people do in the village,
we feature it.

361
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:56,000
Em derbas gundê we Elicaro bûn. Behsa te kirin.
 
We passed through your village Elicaro. They talked about
you.

362
00:22:56,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Gotin tu necarî. Min got em derbas cem te bin.
 
They said you are a carpenter. I said let's visit you.

363
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Bi selamî ehlen wa sehlen, bi xêr hatin ser serê min û ser
çavê min re...
 
With peace, welcome, upon my head and eyes...

364
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Sax be. Ê Apê Xelîl, ka ji berê da ji min re bêje, niha
we... te çi çêdikir ji berê da?
 
Bless you. So Uncle Xelîl, tell me about the past, now...
what did you use to make in the past?

365
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Ji berê da, hencere çêdikir,
 
In the past, I made plows,

366
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Ez kîran çêdikir...
 
I made rakes...

367
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,000
Ez... cerceran çêdikir,
 
I... made threshing sleds,

368
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Ji berê da, yanî min çêdikir, dest te zane.
 
In the past, I mean, I made them, you know.

369
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,000
Ê wa.
 
Yes.

370
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Ê tu ji kê elimîbû, te ji kê fêr bû?
 
So who did you learn from? Who taught you?

371
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
Ez ji kesî neelimîme,
 
I haven't learned from anyone.

372
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Ez bi nerînê me. Ez bi nerînê me, ez li çi binêrim paşê dibe
ji xwe yekê weke wî çêkim.
 
I learned by observing. By observing. Now, whatever I
observe, I can make one like it later.

373
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Ebeden, ez ji kesa neelimîme tu tiştî.
 
Never. I haven't learned anything from anyone.

374
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Ez bi gêcên xwe elimîme.
 
I learned on my own.

375
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Yanî da gund da yan di malbatê da kes tune bûn? Necar tune
bû?
 
So in the village or from the family, there was no one?
There were no carpenters?

376
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:38,000
Na. Di aîleya me da kes jî necar tûne bûn.
 
No, in our family, there are no carpenters either.

377
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,000
Bes ez min. Bi nerînê, yo pê yi tu çi dixwaze, tu çi
dixwaze...
 
It's just me. By observing, stepping by stepping whatever
you want, whatever you want...

378
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:44,000
Bixwe, wek te, ez dizanim, te girt?
 
Did you start it by yourself?

379
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:47,000
Ya, min bixwe girt.
 
Yes, I started it by myself.

380
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Her bijî stêr.
 
Bless you stêr.

381
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Saet te jî xweş be.
 
Bless you too.

382
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Sax be, te got cercer çêdikiri.
 
Bless you. You said you made threshing sleds.

383
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

384
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:58,000
Naha dibêjin cercer, piraniya wan jî nemane.
 
Now they say threshing sleds, most of them aren't around
anymore.

385
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Tine, kêm in.
 
No, they aren't, very few.

386
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:03,000
Ê cercer çend sal naha ev ne, nemane yanî? Berî te bir çend
sal bu?
 
So how many years has it been since the threshing sleds are
no longer around? Before you took it, how many years was it?

387
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Belkî çil sal, penc çil sale,
 
Maybe forty years, forty-five years,

388
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:08,000
sî u pênc, çil e.
 
thirty-five, forty.

389
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:13,000
Nemane. Derasa derketin. Dema derketin, ê wa dewsa cercero
danîn mer.
 
They're gone, combine harvesters came out. When harvesters
came out, they put them instead of threshing sleds.

390
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:20,000
Şuxulê berê bi dewara dikirin. Me qantir dikirin di wan da
wek hev dikirin. Şuxul dikirin.
 
In the past work, we loaded on cattle. We used mules for
both of them. We worked.

391
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:24,000
Ê xwaşîkbûna berê gunda çiqas xweş bû, dema li ser bênder
ha, bi havîna kar-
 
How beautiful the past of the villages was, we used to... on
the threshing floors, in summer working-

392
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,000
Gundî bi xwedê va bi hevra dibûn alîkar...
 
The villagers, by God, helped each other...

393
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:30,000
bi hevra kar dikirin... bi hevra muşaede dikirin, cercera...
 
worked together... supported each other... threshing
sleds...

394
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:34,000
Carek yek xelas bibûya, mesele ez xelas bibûyama eh, cîranî
te bimînya...
 
When someone finished... for instance, if I finished... eh,
your neighbor would be left...

395
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:41,000
El, tu nediçû te xwe belî nedikir. No. Te diçû we re har
gend tekar, wisa dikir.
 
Eh, you wouldn't go and show yourself off. No. You would go
and help them just like you did for yourself.

396
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,000
Yane wek te ji wan re dikir.
 
I mean, you would do it for them just like you did for
yourself.

397
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Yanî bi rastî cercer tê bîra min jî. Dema ez bi zarok bûm li
gund dirûştin.
 
Honestly, you remind me of threshing sleds too. When I was a
child in the village, they used to harvest.

398
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:52,000
Yanî min dît... çawa cercer... di wan deman de derbas
dikirin.
 
I mean, I saw... how threshing sleds... passed through
during that time.

399
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:58,000
Hem ew stranan jî dgotin... cîran û hev ra dibûn alîkar...
yanî xweşikbûyek pir xweşbu.
 
And they even sang songs... neighbors helped each other... I
mean it was a very beautiful thing...

400
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:00,000
Ê, te başqe çi çêkir?
 
So, what else did you make?

401
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:03,000
Min çi çêdikire başqa...
 
What else did I make...

402
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:04,000
waki necariyê.
 
like carpentry.

403
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:10,000
Waki necariyê. Meşt, eh.. tiştan.. wisa... te şite, hanî, tu
tiştê wê çêdikri tişt çêdikir... te çi çêkir...
 
Like carpentry. Brooms, eh... things... like that... you
made tools, brought them, you made things out of wood...
what did you make...

404
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:15,000
Apê Xelîl, dema tu tiştekê çêdikî, tu dişî tu li kî derê
çêdikî? Tu...
 
Uncle Xelîl, when you make something... do you go somewhere
else again... where do you make it? You...

405
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:19,000
Min li gund çêdikir. Li malê, mala min de. Min çêdikiri.
 
I made them in the village. At home, in my home. Made...

406
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:25,000
Ez diçûma çiyê, ez diçûma datim sê car, çar car, hefceyê
yanî dar hişk bûya, di hewşê da.
 
I used to go to the mountains, three times, four times a
week to gather wood when it got dry in the yard.

407
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:27,000
De te zanî, berê hazir tune bû.
 
You know, there wasn't any ready-made stuff back then.

408
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:30,000
Dema ez cut çêdikirim,
 
When I made plows,

409
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:34,000
Min cut çêdikir, ez ez diçûm datim haftake din teşkile din
din, di hewşê da min av dida da hişk nabe.
 
I made plows, I went again the next week to fix the broken
parts, in the yard. I poured water over it so it wouldn't
dry up.

410
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:37,000
Xwedane wê tê, perê xwe dide û dibe.
 
Its owner comes, pays the money and takes it.

411
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:43,000
Ê apê Xelîl naha, wek te, dema te behsa cut kir, ev can wajo
hemi cih in a... kela...
 
Well Uncle Xelîl, just now you were talking about the plows,
what are all those parts... words...

412
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:45,000
Û evên çi zehmetî jî te hebû?
 
And what difficulties did you have with them?

413
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:49,000
Xwê, zehmet... xewî zehmeta wê pir bû. Yanî rihet nebû, pir
zehmet bû.
 
The difficulty... it was very difficult... I mean... not
easy... very hard...

414
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:51,000
Nabe wekî îro, nakabî, na. Îro halet pê derketin a.
 
It's not like today, it's not possible, no. Today tools came
out.

415
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:54,000
Naha kîjan derketiye bi pir rihetî bû. Zehmet nebû.
 
Now, whichever one has come out is very easy. It hasn't been
difficult.

416
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:59,000
Yanî çiqas zihmet biye, em ji wan wek bapîrê me, kalên me,
wê wextê wan nedît. Te dizane?
 
I mean, however difficult it was... our ancestors, our
grandfathers, didn't see that time. Do you know?

417
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Raste, wê demê pir zêdetir zehmet bûn.
 
True, it was much more difficult back then.

418
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:05,000
Dema zeytûn te destan dikir, tu coneyên gir da dikir, te
wisa zeytûna dida der.
 
When you did the olives by hand, you used heavy stones,
that's how you got the olives out.

419
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:14,000
Ev kopçe hebû, kopçe hatin, wê demê kopçe hatin. Vêca wexte
kopçe hatin, derî vekirin, ketin hundir, û ew tiştê di nava
da, wan jî ew derbas kirin.
 
There was a press, the press came, at that time presses
came. So when the press came, they opened the door, went
inside, and those things inside, they also passed them
through.

420
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:16,000
Wê demê te zeytûn çêdikir?
 
Did you make olives at that time?

421
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:19,000
Le va paşê zeytûn qudkirin d'çandin,
 
Yes, later they planted olives,

422
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:21,000
U di wê çaxê da cortî di vir de tune bû,
 
And during those times we had plows here,

423
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Di wê çaxê da traktor tune bûn, dar tune bû, cot bû, cût di
vir da bû.
 
in those times tractors didn't exist, there were no
tractors, there were plows, pairs of plows.

424
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Eh, cût da cotkar. Ferqek pir heye niha wisa ye...
 
Yes, they plowed with plows. There is a huge difference
now...

425
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:34,000
Bes kîjan dem, ew dem xwastir e yan îro xwastir e?
 
But which time is better, that time or today?

426
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:36,000
Wella wê demê xweş bû, ne.
 
Well, those times were nice, yes.

427
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:38,000
Ji aliyê şirînî, piramîn ji bav ra alîkar dikirin.
 
We used to help each other with a lot of love..

428
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:42,000
Lê ew dem e, cûtên heywanan, niha hola ye... bi xweştî...
Niha emrê min heftê sal e.
 
But that time... the animal plows, now it's a piece of
cake... with ease... Now, I am seventy years old.

429
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Sibê tu te digire, da ta êvarê tu davêje ser. Tu aciz nabî.
 
Tomorrow you start, until evening you keep doing it. You
don't get bored.

430
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Ez jî aciz nabim.
 
I don't get bored either.

431
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:50,000
Xwezî wextê berê da, te cût dajot,
 
I wish it was like the old days, when you plowed,

432
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:55,000
Keft ta ew da te naxwe, ewe di ew tu li ki tûftelî.
 
Sometimes they wouldn't go, so you would stop and tell them
to turn around.

433
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Sekenî ra ker, ser we tu siwar dibî... te te dîtî...
 
When they stopped, you would get on them... you saw that...

434
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:04,000
Niha kêlapeta aro... nav ko dikî dar bi dest e ko gi xera
bike...
 
Now it's easy... inside the plow, a piece of wood in your
hand to clear it up...

435
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:09,000
jor û jor de du car dike u hin jî dibin axê... dû qena
derbale mena wan e.
 
you do it up and up twice, and they go into the soil... so
you can use it again like that.

436
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:14,000
Yanî ne wekî ya berê ye. Ya çaxê te cotkê te dor dirove.
 
I mean, it's not like the old days. When it was your turn to
plow, the plowing went around.

437
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:16,000
Em vegerin ser karê te.
 
Let's focus on your work now.

438
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:22,000
Niha te li pêşî min pir tişt hene, kîja ti bixwe tiştekî,
ser karê xwe deng kî?
 
Now you have a lot of items in front of me, could you
explain each of them, talk about your work?

439
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:26,000
Ev? Ev tûmeqa. Ma tu tûmeqê ji bo çi bikar tînî? Zehtûn a?
 
This? This is a mallet. What do you use the mallet for?
Olives?

440
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:27,000
Ji bo zeytûn e.
 
It is for olives.

441
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:32,000
Me'nî pîrek, an ji, jinek bîr da ew zeytûna bişkîne.
 
Mostly an old woman, or a woman would use it to crack the
olives.

442
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:34,000
Ji bo zeytûn, a.
 
For olives, yes.

443
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:39,000
Û ev jî... Sîrge ye. Ev ji wextê berê.
 
And this is... A rolling pin. This is from the old days.

444
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Zemanê berê, mehkûm... gundî tiştek di malan de tune bû.
 
In the old days, people... the villagers didn't have much in
their homes.

445
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:49,000
Wê çaxê ha ew darî bû. Hev darî bû. Bi dest da şixulî. Yanî
çi xwêr be bi wî der de diki.
 
At that time, it was made of wood. Everything was made of
wood. We worked by hand. I mean, whatever food there was,
you used this.

446
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Ha ew tişt hebû. Hev jî kefçî ye. Ew bi darê şîp ê bû. Hev
ji wisa ji dehan e, dehan bû.
 
This thing existed. This is a spoon. It was made from wood.
This is also from the ten, it was from the ten.

447
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:57,000
Wê demê hemî kefçî ê dar bûn.
 
At that time all the spoons were made of wood.

448
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:59,000
Belê. Ê dar bûn.
 
Yes. They were made of wood.

449
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:01,000
Ev kijan dar in, taybet, dar e kijan dar e?
 
Which wood are these, specifically, which wood is it?

450
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:03,000
Ev dare qetleb e ye.
 
This is arbutus wood.

451
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:05,000
Ev kefçî, yane darê şîf ê.
 
This spoon, it's a soup spoon.

452
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:08,000
Em çêdikin, jinan bi şîf tewdidin. Pêdikarin.
 
We make them, women cook soup with them. They manage it.

453
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:11,000
Heha nuha bikar tînin?
 
Are they still using it now?

454
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Are, nuha bikar tînin, yanî ê ku dixwaze bikar tîne... Ew jî
hez dike bikar tîne bi vî karî kar tîne... wê tînin pê da tu
ew nakî kefçekî dar da dixwazin hewe tîne. Ew jê naha.
Kefçên derketiye aluminium, tûştî wan tînin. Ê... pakî ew
qet hez nake.
 
Yes, they still use it, I mean whoever wants to uses it...
Whoever likes it uses it for this purpose... if you don't do
that, they want a wooden spoon and bring it. That one from
now. Spoons made of aluminum have come out, they bring
those. Yeah... absolutely nobody likes that.

455
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:34,000
Heveb se zire, per xwendi... Ev tişt te bi destê xwe
çêkiriye. Te tiştek din dîtiye? Tu tişt te dîtiye... ne ew
tişt min ne dîtiye...
 
Those things are strong, they look nice... You made this by
hand. Have you seen anything else? You have seen anything...
no I haven't seen that...

456
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Te bi destê xwe çêkiriye.
 
You made it by hand.

457
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:44,000
Ev kefçe da te li qetlabeyê ye. Me'ne deye. Va ji wi çoqtir
cêye. Ev ji quçe mezine. Zêde mezine... o mezin ji hene..
 
This spoon is from arbutus wood. Mostly yes. This one is
smaller. This is also a big spoon. It's quite big... there
are big ones as well..

458
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:46,000
U mezin jî hene?
 
And there are big ones as well?

459
00:28:46,000 --> 00:29:00,000
U mezin jî hene. Arî. O hebok, min tiştek çekir, mine fireh
jî, fira ca. Ti dî se dî sîni dinê, zordar ti key hana
bikî... le xe hewike sehke... car jibo goştê avê. Ena jibo
goşt.
 
And there are big ones as well. Yes. That small one, I made
something, something wide too, wide ones. You know, you hit
it, put it on top, look hard at it... sometimes for watery
meat. Or for meat.

460
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Ebo jibo goşt... evî me ne jibo ker... evî me çêkir jibo
malê, evî em me dewarek xweşe cekir a. Mîrov hewce dike
nebin.
 
Oh, for meat... this is mostly for cutting... we made this
for home, we made this one for nice animals. People
shouldn't be needy.

461
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:32,000
Seheke te te ji per çiye.. per cuce... heho deheye.. hebo
jeme hebu... le hebu ke curike ew uşt he ki ra peş de keri
hêsan an pe di kinir hewo diker, sor diker eho we ez en tew
sor naki ji. Mase keri nav be... em esra di keri na de we ji
urs se na, naha te bi dewi... ew de... ev wate de hebe u se
heb o caqo ke a va hewa ji se ew de oheye na. A heye ca.
 
Look, see how much you... how much... this is what we have..
this is what we had... or what it was... they cut it easily
or cut it, fry it but I won't fry it. Cut it like this... we
fry it... I cut it, right... this... this means something or
cut it.. or it's there. That's it.

462
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:56,000
Te ji med xewe de ye. Hev med xewe de ye.. reşa ene qulad a
der hewa hene.. heni ta te ki reş ni vek mi reş peş ew den
bula da di der heve ne.. ta.. vek i reke di hene de ne...
bova ji per ser di ki de ew de ki em pe çekeri hav deker e.
 
You gave yourself to it. Gave yourself to it... black ones,
there's wood under them... even if you turn the black to
front, they put it there.. up.. until it gets there... you
get it done and we make it, right.

463
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Nuha o teqeli...
 
Now the ceiling...

464
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:03,000
Dema dar û berên we zil dibûn, we dalîvek çêdikir?
 
When you ran out of wood, did you make a dalîv?

465
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:04,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

466
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Dalîvên we ji çi bûn, te bi xwe çêdikirî, yan kesekî ji te
re çêdikirî?
 
What were your dalîvs made of, did you make them yourself,
or did someone make them for you?

467
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:08,000
Welleh dalîvên me karî reş e, beriyê çêdikirin.
 
Well, our dalîvs were made of 'karî reş' (black thorny
bushes), they used to make them in the past.

468
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:13,000
Xelkê hejar hebûn, ew a dikirin, ya reş çêdikirin û
difirotin.
 
There were poor people, they used to gather the black
bushes, make them, and sell them.

469
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Qesdîkê di malên xelfan hebûn, li kûra wan çêdikir.
 
They had 'qesdîk' in the houses of the brickmakers, where
they made them.

470
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Diçûn ji Lîçê sênara çêdikirin.
 
They used to go and make sênar from Lîçê.

471
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:22,000
Na te dît? Ev dikirin ha, çêdikirin wilo, çêdikirin.
 
You see? They used to do this, make them like that.

472
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Kevirî ji biniya vê ra dibêjin sênî? Ewa sêniyê biniyê ye.
 
The stone at the bottom of it, is it called 'sênî'? It's the
bottom 'sênî'.

473
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:27,000
Yanî, ne te çêdikirî?
 
So, you didn't make it?

474
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:28,000
Na, me çênedikirî.
 
No, we didn't make them.

475
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Na, xelkê hejar hebûn, wan a çêdikirin.
 
No, there were poor people, they used to make them.

476
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:35,000
Qesdîkê di malê xelfan, ebdê di malê xelfan jî wan
çêdikirin.
 
Qesdîk in the houses of the brickmakers, the servants in the
brickmakers' houses also made them.

477
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:38,000
Lê wekî tu rojên li gundekî bûyî, gundê Qurnê bûyî.
 
But as you were in a village, the village of Qurne.

478
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Yek ji xwe ji gundî bi xwe dalîva çêkiribû yanî?
 
Didn't anyone from the village make their own dalîv?

479
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:44,000
Erê. O poşî em difitilîn.
 
Yes. Then we used to turn it.

480
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:48,000
Me ox dikirinê, ox darikî wilo xwar e, darê merxê xwar e, av
wilo diketî...
 
We used to make an 'ox', an 'ox' is a piece of wood like
this, bent, it's bent wood of an oak tree, it would fit like
that...

481
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:49,000
Me çêdikirin.
 
We used to make them.

482
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:52,000
Hê em li se dewêr dikirine, li du dawêr dawereke gênd bû,
dawêr bû.
 
We used to put them on the animals, behind the animals it
was a round loop.

483
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Hene li gunda heye îro?
 
Are there any in the village today?

484
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:57,000
Hey e, lê teb'en heye. Gundakî de heye.
 
Yes, of course there are. There are in some villages.

485
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Ma we bi xwe qet tahwî çêkirî?
 
Did you ever make tahwi yourself?

486
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Na, me qet çênekiriye.
 
No, we never made it.

487
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:01,000
Spas ji te ra, saetxweş.
 
Thank you, have a good time.

488
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Saetxweş be, Xwedê ji te razî be. Silav be.
 
Have a good time, may God bless you. Greetings.

489
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:11,000
Spas.
 
Thanks.

490
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:17,000
Li başûrê herdu gundan, gundê Mistanşûra û Çiyayê Eiyê Omê,
yekû bedar û ber in...
 
South of both villages, the village of Mistanşûra and Mount
Eiyê Omê, together with trees and stones...

491
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:21,000
...merx e, rengê kes di hemû demsalan da xwe dide kevê...
 
...are oak trees, its green color shows itself to the
partridge in all seasons...

492
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:24,000
...û li bakurê gund, Bîrkan e.
 
...and to the north of the village is Bîrkan.

493
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Li rojavayê gund, Cumê Zînay e...
 
To the west of the village is Cumê Zînay...

494
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:28,000
...ew jî nêzîktirîn gund e...
 
...it is also the closest village...

495
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:48,000
...û li rojava gundê Şiketa ye.
 
...and to the west is the village of Shiketa.

496
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:16,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja...
 
Yes, dear viewers...

497
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:19,000
Di gundê Raca da jî em rastî malekê hatin, ew jî...
 
In the village of Raca, we also came across a family, and
they also...

498
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:24,000
Êzinga hûr dikin ji bo zivistana, hazirtiya xwe sibeha
dikin.
 
Are chopping wood for the winter, preparing themselves for
tomorrow.

499
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Niha jî em dê bi wan ra nas bikin. Merheba ji we ra.
 
Now we will get to know them. Hello to you.

500
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:28,000
Merheba.
 
Hello.

501
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:29,000
Em we nas bikin.
 
Let us get to know you.

502
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Remzî navê min.
 
Remzi is my name.

503
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Navê min Henan e.
 
Upon my eyes.

504
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:32,000
Navê min Henan e.
 
My name is Henan.

505
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Ser çavê min. Û tu ji kîjan gundî yî?
 
Upon my eyes. And which village are you from?

506
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Gundê Raca ne.
 
The village of Raca.

507
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:37,000
Gundê Raca ne.
 
The village of Raca.

508
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:40,000
Ew roj be û germe, li gundan wilo ye, di gundê El Cariya da
berdewam e.
 
It's a sunny and hot day, it's like this in the villages, it
continues in the village of El Cariya.

509
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Em rast hatin, vî jî êzinga hûr dikin.
 
We came across them, they are also chopping wood.

510
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:45,000
Kesê hûr dike jî em ê bi wî nas bikin.
 
We will also get to know the person who is chopping.

511
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Heysem.
 
Heysem.

512
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Heysem e, ev ê Remzî ye.
 
Your name?

513
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:48,000
Heysem e, ev ê Remzî ye.
 
It's Heysem, this is Remzi.

514
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:52,000
Ser çavên min. Detsên we sax bin, spas ji te re jî.
 
Upon my eyes. Bless your hands, thank you too.

515
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:55,000
Niha dema êzingan e, û zivistan e...
 
Now is the time for wood, and it is winter...

516
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:59,000
We dest bi zivistanê kiriye û we serma çêbûye.
 
Winter has started for you and you have cold weather.

517
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:03,000
Vêca hazirtiya xwe dikin di vê çaxê da.
 
So you are making preparations at this time.

518
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:05,000
Berê çawa bû? Gava hûn diçûn zivistanê...
 
How was it in the past? When you were heading into winter...

519
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:08,000
Ji berê da, em bi sobehiyê bûn.
 
In the past, we had stoves.

520
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:10,000
Ronahî jî qolikên me ducan girtin...
 
As for light, we held double lanterns...

521
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:12,000
Ji gundê qalên me dihatin, ducan girtin.
 
They came from our tribal village, holding double.

522
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:14,000
Bes berê, me sobe tê de nebû...
 
But in the past, we didn't have stoves inside...

523
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,000
Çal hebûn, ji bo me çêkirin...
 
There were pits, made for us...

524
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Diçûn, merxê wenda dikirin, dihatin li kêleka qalikan...
 
They went, gathered branches, came and stood next to the
bark...

525
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:20,000
...di nav de dikirin qolinc, weha. Dikirin qolinc...
 
...and tied them into bundles, like this. They tied them
into bundles...

526
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:22,000
...ji pûxarê, metrekî pixarê bû.
 
...for the chimney, it was a one-meter chimney.

527
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Ew ji bo pûxarê bû?
 
Was that for the chimney?

528
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:24,000
Pûxare bû lê, dikirin pixarê li vir diket.
 
It was a chimney, yes, they put it in the chimney and it
would drop here.

529
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Di rûyê asê ra, ew diçû dihate binî.
 
Through the steep surface, it went down to the bottom.

530
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Ber poxarê jî xirê dibû, negeriya, yek ve bû, yek wî bû.
Bes.
 
Around the chimney there would be debris, it didn't turn,
one was like this, one was his. That's it.

531
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:31,000
E milatê din li kû da diçûn?
 
Where did the other people go?

532
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,000
Milatê din parve dikirin, cih tunebû...
 
The other people distributed it, there was no space...

533
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Wê ew bes êzing germ dikirin yan na?
 
Did that wood only heat up, or not?

534
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:39,000
Germ dikir lê, nabe wekî soba germ dikir.
 
It heated up, yes, but it wasn't like how a stove heated.

535
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Ewa germ bûn, ew wer da dihat, dê derneket. Şûna... evê germ
dibû ew der.
 
It got warm, it would fall down, it wouldn't come out. The
place... that place would get warm.

536
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:49,000
Berê wisa, we dît hinek tiştê berê pir fireh bûn...
 
In the past, you saw that some things in the past were very
wide...

537
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:53,000
Pir fireh bûn, lê wî berê wisa nediketiye nika bû, fireh
bûn, germ nedibûn...
 
They were very wide, yes, but before it wasn't like now,
they were wide, they wouldn't get warm...

538
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Xaniyek dîrokî bû, fireh bû, germ nedibû.
 
It was a historical house, it was wide, it wouldn't get
warm.

539
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:58,000
Çîrok û... çîmentoyê sora...
 
Story and... red cement...

540
00:33:58,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Berê dirokî bû... Û yekî me bihêrî bû, bi axê bû.
 
It was historical before... And we had one that was crushed,
made of dirt.

541
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Ar di nav de xweş dihatin. Dema di nava de dixist, di hundir
de germ dibû.
 
Fire was nice inside. When it was put inside, it would get
warm inside.

542
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:12,000
Û paşî bi dorê da hatin, yanî dudu em li ber poxarê
rûniştin...
 
And then they came in turn, meaning we two sat by the
chimney...

543
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:16,000
...me bi dorê da ew diçû jî yanî. Hew wisa dihatin
rûdiniştin.
 
...we took turns and it would pass. They would come and sit
like that.

544
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Bi vî awayî derbas dikirin.
 
They passed it in this way.

545
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:22,000
Piştî wê, tiştên derbas bûn, çûn da hatin, bûn tiştên ecêb.
 
After that, the things that passed, they came and went, they
became strange things.

546
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:28,000
Mazot hat... yanî, ew tişta... te dît we tişt her tişt zêde
bû.
 
Diesel came... meaning, that thing... you saw that
everything increased.

547
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Basî we sobeya êzingan çima nemaye?
 
But why is the wood stove not left?

548
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Sobeya êzingan?
 
The wood stove?

549
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:32,000
Wê nema ye...
 
It's not left...

550
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:37,000
Piştî dema reş... fokî zivistanan mêş dîtin, mêş.
 
After the black era... during the winters they saw mice,
mice.

551
